# Raw agent transcripts. Private by default at every capture preset
# (ADR-0005 Decision 2); publishing one is a separate escalation needing two
# independent opt-ins. Anchored so it matches this directory only — an
# unanchored "runs/" matches at any depth and silently swept up stats/runs/.
/runs/

# Scratch space for in-flight journal work. Deliberately left unanchored: it
# was, and changing that would alter what is publishable without a decision.
tmp/

# Per-run logs alongside transcripts.
*.log

# v1-schema per-run statistics from the legacy stats tooling. Local working
# data, not evidence: the journal's own session records are the supported
# economics and are published with the rest of the journal. Scoped to runs/
# alone — stats/evaluations/ is a configured store (config/runtime.conf) whose
# publication status is not this rule's to decide.
/stats/runs/
